      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: bouncemarket – a live prediction market game for a bouncing ball",
      "url": "https://bouncemarket.minhanhday.com/",
      "author": "mday404",
      "external_id": "50667726",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-27T15:01:50Z",
      "score": 169,
      "comments": 45,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50667726",
      "snippet": "a ball will fall. trade on where it lands.<p>I made this game! Some technical details:<p>The entire drop of the ball is simulated server-side, then streamed to each client as server-sent events with a small buffer. Every drop is deterministic from its starting position, so rounds can be replayed exactly for later analysis, but tiny variations in starting position can change the ultimate outcome.<p>There&#x27;s some AI traders to keep the market moving, but they drop out in any round that has more than five people. They operate using a naive set of rules that I wrote for them, so they&#x27;re not too hard to beat -- it&#x27;s when the market is full of real people that it gets tricky.<p>Curious to get feedback on anything you would change, and especially whether the mechanics were clear right away or not.",
      "links": []
